@startuml GITGLE Complete Data Flow Diagram
title GITGLE: Complete End-to-End Data Flow

participant User
participant CLI as "CLI/index.js"
participant CrawlPipeline as "Crawl Pipeline"
participant GitHubAPI as "GitHub API\nService"
participant RepoDataFetcher as "Repo Data\nFetcher"
participant MapReduceCrawl as "MapReduce\nValidation"
participant Store as "Distributed\nStore"
participant IndexPipeline as "Index\nPipeline"
participant MapReduceIndex as "MapReduce\nIndexing"
participant RankingEngine as "Ranking\nEngine"
participant SearchPipeline as "Search\nPipeline"
participant QueryProcessor as "Query\nProcessor"
participant RankingSearch as "Ranking\nEngine"

== INITIALIZATION ==
User -> CLI: npm start
activate CLI
CLI -> CrawlPipeline: Start crawl

== CRAWL PHASE ==
activate CrawlPipeline
CrawlPipeline -> CrawlPipeline: Load seed repos (114)
CrawlPipeline -> RepoDataFetcher: fetchRepoData(seed)

activate RepoDataFetcher
RepoDataFetcher -> GitHubAPI: getRepositoryDocument()
activate GitHubAPI
GitHubAPI -> GitHubAPI: Fetch metadata\n(stars, language, description)
GitHubAPI -> GitHubAPI: Fetch README.md\nfrom raw.githubusercontent.com
GitHubAPI -> RepoDataFetcher: Return {metadata, readme}
deactivate GitHubAPI

RepoDataFetcher -> Store: Store repo document\n{key: 'repo:owner/name', gid: 'gitgle'}
activate Store
Store -> Store: Consistent hash\nShards data
deactivate Store
RepoDataFetcher -> CrawlPipeline: callback(null, repoData)
deactivate RepoDataFetcher

CrawlPipeline -> MapReduceCrawl: runJob(114 repos)
activate MapReduceCrawl
MapReduceCrawl -> MapReduceCrawl: Map: Extract repo\nmetadata from each
MapReduceCrawl -> MapReduceCrawl: Shuffle: Group by\nrepo owner
MapReduceCrawl -> MapReduceCrawl: Reduce: Validate\nall repos stored
MapReduceCrawl -> Store: Store metadata\nkeys list\n{key: 'crawl:all-metadata-keys'}
MapReduceCrawl -> CrawlPipeline: Return 114 successful
deactivate MapReduceCrawl

CrawlPipeline -> CLI: Crawl complete callback
deactivate CrawlPipeline

== INDEX PHASE ==
CLI -> IndexPipeline: Start index

activate IndexPipeline
IndexPipeline -> Store: Get crawl:all-metadata-keys\n(114 repo keys)
activate Store
Store -> IndexPipeline: Return keys list
deactivate Store

IndexPipeline -> RankingEngine: Initialize TF-IDF\ncalculator
activate RankingEngine
RankingEngine -> RankingEngine: Load totalDocs = 114\nPrepare metadata boost\nfactors

IndexPipeline -> MapReduceIndex: runJob(114 documents)
activate MapReduceIndex

MapReduceIndex -> MapReduceIndex: For each document:
MapReduceIndex -> MapReduceIndex: 1. Fetch from Store\n2. Tokenize README\n3. Stem terms\n4. Count frequencies

MapReduceIndex -> RankingEngine: Calculate TF-IDF\nfor each term
RankingEngine -> RankingEngine: For each term:\ntf × log(totalDocs/docFreq)\n× metadata_boost

MapReduceIndex -> MapReduceIndex: Build inverted index:\n{term: {postings: [...],\ndocumentFrequency: N,\ntfIdfScores: {docId: score}}}

MapReduceIndex -> Store: Store inv:full-index\n(4415 unique terms)\n{key: 'inv:full-index', gid: 'gitgle'}
activate Store
Store -> Store: Persist to\ndistributed\nstorage
deactivate Store

MapReduceIndex -> IndexPipeline: Return index stats
deactivate MapReduceIndex

IndexPipeline -> CLI: Index complete callback
deactivate RankingEngine
deactivate IndexPipeline

== SEARCH PHASE ==
User -> CLI: Enter search query\n"python"

activate SearchPipeline
CLI -> SearchPipeline: executeSearch("python", {...})

SearchPipeline -> Store: Get inv:full-index
activate Store
Store -> SearchPipeline: Return full inverted index
deactivate Store

SearchPipeline -> QueryProcessor: Parse query
activate QueryProcessor
QueryProcessor -> QueryProcessor: Tokenize: ["python"]\nStem: ["python"]
QueryProcessor -> SearchPipeline: Return processed terms
deactivate QueryProcessor

SearchPipeline -> SearchPipeline: In-memory lookup:\ninv_index["python"]

SearchPipeline -> SearchPipeline: Get postings list:\n[{repoId, freq, tfIdfScore}, ...]

SearchPipeline -> RankingSearch: Calculate final scores\nfor each result
activate RankingSearch
RankingSearch -> RankingSearch: Apply metadata boosts:\n- Language boost (1.3×)\n- Stars boost (1.2-2.0×)
RankingSearch -> RankingSearch: Final score =\ntfIdfScore × boosts
RankingSearch -> SearchPipeline: Return ranked results
deactivate RankingSearch

SearchPipeline -> Store: Fetch repo metadata\nfor each result
activate Store
Store -> SearchPipeline: Return {owner, repo,\nstars, language, desc}
deactivate Store

SearchPipeline -> SearchPipeline: Extract snippets\nfrom README
SearchPipeline -> SearchPipeline: Clean markdown:\nRemove images, links,\ntables, code blocks
SearchPipeline -> SearchPipeline: Sort by score\nLimit to top 10
SearchPipeline -> SearchPipeline: Format results

SearchPipeline -> CLI: Return ranked results
deactivate SearchPipeline

CLI -> User: Display:\n1. django-rest-framework (38.278) ⭐\n2. aiohttp (7.656) ⭐\n...

@enduml
